# Merge drivers for the ledgers that slices append to (slice BL1b, 20 November 2026).
#
# ADR_RESERVATIONS.md takes git's union merge: two branches that each append a reservation row both
# keep it, instead of bouncing the merge. This is safe for this file alone, because its changes are row
# appends at the end. The one in-place edit it sees is a status flip of a row from "reserved" to
# "written", and a flip made two ways, or any other edit to a row, is what union would double or let
# through; the checks catch both: tools/adr_reservations_check.py reports a number reserved twice and
# a doubled row (tests/test_adr_reservations.py), and its --against mode compares the file with the
# merge-base and allows only appended rows and that one flip (tests/test_ledger_union_merge.py).
#
# spec/06_DECISIONS.md is NOT listed. Its amendments are appended blocks, but it also has content edited
# in place (the status register near the top, and amendment bodies edited more than once), and when two
# branches edit the same line union keeps both versions, so the line would be doubled. Adding it needs
# the duplicate-heading and doubled-line checks on main first, and the owner's word.
#
# The attributes are read from the tree being merged, so this applies to every merge into main once the
# file is on main; a branch that brings the file in does not get it for its own merge of main.
OspreyFlow_Build/spec/ADR_RESERVATIONS.md merge=union
